WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.640
- His name is Ever, is that
short for something or what?

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.030
- No, Ever is a name
that I just always loved

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.680
and it's funny, 'cause
you were talking about

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.250
your Italian family and you
and I have talked a lot about

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.710
coming from these very big
and vibrant Italian families.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.970
So it's always part of
the family tradition

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.870
that we tell what the name is

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.530
and that everyone can be
involved in the decision

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.490
and of course, they wanted to use

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.840
all of the existing family names,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.470
like my cousin is Gina Nicole
and her sister's Nicole Gina

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.330
and then there's Thomas Anthony,

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.660
Anthony Thomas and they were like,

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.240
aren't you gonna name the baby, Anthony?

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.646
I'm like, we have 10 Anthonys.

00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:36.479
(audience laughs)

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:39.130
I think it's good, but
they love the name, Ever,

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.550
when they found out what it was,

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.010
except it's actually sounding
a little bit more like Eva,

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:45.843
it's for my--

00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:47.010
Eva, you know, Eva!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:48.893
With the accents.

00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:50.620
- Yeah, now where does
it come from though?

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.453
- [Female Speaker] The name?

00:00:51.453 --> 00:00:53.061
- Yeah, how did you
come up with that name?

00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:54.530
- I don't remember I think I'm probably

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.480
found it on a baby name
blog or something like that.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.620
- Well, see I'd never heard
that as a name until your child.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.200
- Okay, actually we'll say that

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.070
Alanis Morissette son's name was, Ever,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.160
and I loved it so much when
I heard that she had it,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.120
so I sort of stole it.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.936
- Oh, ah-hah, ah-hah!

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:12.887
- Oh no, I can believe I just said that!

00:01:12.887 --> 00:01:13.873
(Female speaker chuckles)

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.722
- All right, now we see how
we get to the truth here.

00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:17.580
- I don't even think
my husband knows that.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.413
- [Male Speaker] Really?

00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:19.520
- No!
- [Male Speaker] Wow!

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.353
- I was just like,

00:01:20.353 --> 00:01:22.440
I came up with it on my
own, I had a dream about it.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.426
That's what I should've said,
it came to me in a dream.

00:01:24.426 --> 00:01:26.130
- Okay, okay, well it's too late now.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:26.963
- I know.

